ulus_multiplication_and_product_27e68640_011_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Using $7\\times19=7(20-1)$, what value follows from distributivity?","options":["$140$","$126$","$137$","$133$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"384b6539509111b39e7260a4","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_050_multiplication_and_product_add_003_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why must $(-1)(-1)=1$ hold for real numbers?","options":["It is forced by distributivity, absorbing zero and $a\\cdot1=a$","It is a separate convention, not forced by the other laws","Commutativity lets the two minus signs swap and cancel","It follows from the identity law $a\\cdot1=a$ alone"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a0bab9995e0ddabcbea127d1","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_050_multiplication_and_product_add_007_curated20261027_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which set is closed under multiplication, i.e. contains $ab$ whenever it contains $a$ and $b$?","options":["$\\{0,1\\}$","The negative integers","The irrational numbers","$\\{1,2\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"426de8c972a178eeaa969801","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_050_multiplication_and_product_add_008_curated20261027_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $a<b$ be real numbers. For which multiplier $c$ does $ca>cb$ hold?","options":["$c=-2$","$c=2$","$c=0$","$c=1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ec2bde864438b8349660c515","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_multiplication_and_product_27e68640_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which expression equals $(a+b)(c+d)$ for all real numbers $a$, $b$, $c$, $d$?","options":["$ac+ad+bc+bd$","$ac+bd$","$ac+2ad+bd$","$a(c+d)+b$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bf07e792366cfad3db9b0dff","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_multiplication_and_product_27e68640_topup20261028_002","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $a$, $b$ and $x$ be real numbers with $ax<bx$, where nothing is known about the sign of $x$. Which conclusion is correct?","options":["$a<b$, since the common factor $x\\neq0$ can be cancelled.","$a<b$ and $x>0$, since a negative $x$ would flip the inequality.","$x\\neq0$; then $a<b$ if $x>0$, and $a>b$ if $x<0$.","Nothing follows, since for $x=0$ the numbers $a,b$ are arbitrary."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"645dde3eaa9b73727821dadc","time_limit":45}]}}